#!/bin/sh
# fnOS creates the container from the packaged compose BEFORE this callback
# and its package scripts run without docker socket access (real-device
# finding: permission denied). So this only renders the compose for the
# platform's own (re)create, never tries to drive docker itself.
set -eu
sh "$(dirname "$0")/prepare"
printf '%s install: compose rendered for the platform\n' "$(date '+%F %T')" >> "$TRIM_PKGVAR/info.log" 2>/dev/null || true
exit 0
